Example configuration for the ``moat ems sched`` optimizer.

The scheduler is driven by a YAML config file (see ``params.yaml``) that
selects pluggable data loaders for price, solar, and load forecasts, sets
the battery / inverter / grid hardware limits, and chooses where to write
results.

Run the optimizer from this folder (so the relative data-file paths in
``params.yaml`` resolve):

    moat ems sched -c params.yaml analyze --force

``--force`` skips the "you must be near a timeslot boundary" check; drop it
when running on the hour in production. Add ``--all`` to emit the full
multi-period trajectory instead of just the first interval.

Input data files (one float per line, in kW / $ per kWh):

- ``price.data``  — sell prices per hour
- ``solar.data`` — projected solar power per hour
- ``load.data``  — projected local consumption per hour

Buy prices are derived from the sell prices by the ``file2`` mode:
``price_buy = factor * price_sell + offset`` (here ``1.2 * price + 0.24``,
equivalent to ``(price + 0.2) * 1.2``).
